#HELPS

0 COLORS COLOURS~
Syntax: colors
        colors <purple|red|blue|green|yellow|black>
Sorcerer/Chaos Book Mage color training. Displays the six current tracks,
or trains one for 10 times its next rank in primal. Each track caps at 5.
The sphere Mage SPHERE command is a different progression system.
~

0 SORCCREATE~
Syntax: sorccreate starter
        sorccreate <book|page|pen>
Sorcerers can claim one free starter kit with instructions, tools and the
ready-to-chant Spark, Mend and Minor Ward spells. Existing color mastery
is preserved; repeated claims are refused and the claim is saved.
Separate crafted books and pens cost 10 primal each; pages have no primal
fee. Crafting requires the native protoplasm object template.
Chaos Book Mages create Chaos books; they remain one Sorcerer parent variant.
~

0 VISION~
Syntax: vision
Sorcerer enhanced-vision toggle. Uses native holy-light, shadowsight and
night-sight flags, and removes those flags when toggled off.
It is not Mage Nightsight, another class's discipline or a movement power.
~

0 ENCHANT~
Syntax: enchant <carried weapon or armor>
Sorcerer enchantment adds permanent object affects of +5 hitroll and
+5 damroll, then marks QUEST_SORCENCHANT to prevent repeated copies.
The native command rejects other item types, artifacts and already
Sorcerer-enchanted items. It has no separate mana/primal payment.
This is not MAGEENCHANT or the restricted Enchant Weapon/Armor callbacks.
~

0 WRITE~
Syntax: write <carried page/book> title <text>
        write <carried page> line <text>
Hold a pen first. Books accept titles; pages accept titles and appended
lines. Existing line-length limits still apply. Mundane writing is not
restricted to Sorcerers, but ordinary non-Sorcerer writing does not grant
working spell craftsmanship.
Spell pages must follow the native ordered grammar and finish correctly.
Read the starter primer, HELP BOOKWRITING and HELP BOOKRECIPE;
arbitrary prose is not a spell.
~

0 CHANT BOOKCHANT~
Syntax: chant <target required by the selected spell>
Hold an open spellbook, TURN to a finished spell page and then CHANT.
For starter spells use CHANT <opponent> for Spark, CHANT SELF for Mend
and Minor Ward. Reading/lesson/index pages are not executable spells.
Silence, an incomplete/failed page, missing targets, insufficient mana,
native immunity/protection and existing same-color effects can block a cast.
Costs, targets and effects depend on the page's compiled spell type/color.
Native page chains stop at their ten-page recursion limit.
~

0 BOOKRECIPE SPELLWRITING~
Native spell-writing outline:
Hold a pen; create/carry a page; use WRITE <page> LINE <one directive>.
Begin with exactly one of:
  start.damage.spell
  start.affect.spell
  start.action.spell
Affect pages can add APPLY: hp/mana/armor/hitroll/damroll/save,
AFFECT: blind/umbra/sanct/faerie.fire/curse/flaming/poison/sleep/web,
DURATION: <0..50>, and REVERSED to reverse stat bonuses.
Optional MESSAGE.1:, MESSAGE.2: and MESSAGE.3: set native cast messages.
Finish with END.PURPLE/RED/BLUE/GREEN/YELLOW/BLACK, or END.RANDOM.
Type one complete directive per line; do not type the slash-separated lists.
Invalid/out-of-order/duplicate directives can mark the page failed.
Insert the page into an open book with CAST 'INSERT PAGE' <page> <book>,
hold the book, TURN to that page and CHANT the appropriate target.
Use the starter primer for a complete worked example and role differences.
Armor bonuses are positive in Genesis; REVERSED makes a positive stat
bonus negative. Existing historical saved pages are not rewritten.
~

0 CHAOSBOOKS CHAOSPAGES~
Chaos Book Mage is a Sorcerer variant, not an extra standalone parent.
Join using AUTOCLASS SORCERER CHAOS (or the CHAOSMAGE alias).
Its book chooses a fresh color when a page is chanted, rather than fixing
that page permanently to its prior color. Repeated rolls may repeat colors.
The implemented Chaos handling preserves the page's attack/healing/affect
role; a blessing does not become an attack just because its color changed.
Color mastery, mana, target checks and normal book restrictions still apply.
~

